  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TAIMAKO COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT INITIATIVE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project entitled: Improving Community Food Security and Livelihoods through Farming for Resilience (F4R) is a 30,000 project that is directly targeting 360 vulnerable households (approximately 1,800 individuals) mostly women and youth ages 18 -30 years including persons with disability across selected food-insecure communities in Kano State, Nigeria. The project equips vulnerable households to produce a variety of nutrient-dense foods locally by distributing vital farming inputs, building capacity, and utilising climate-smart agricultural practices.</narrative>
  </description>
